# WHAT PRETTIER MAY NOT TOUCH. Every line here decides something — prettier 3
# already honours .gitignore, so build output and scratch directories need no
# entry and none is given.

# D14 — A MERGED DRAWING IS IMMUTABLE. These are the design sessions' own
# output, cited by line number from code comments and decisions. Measured with
# THIS config: `period-and-analytics.dc.html` goes from 2 729 lines to 7 535,
# a 7 152-line rewrite of a file the repo has promised not to edit.
design/

# EVERY Markdown file, at every depth — not just the root, and not just docs/.
# The plans, decisions, reference notes and the folder READMEs are all
# hand-formatted prose whose tables carry measured figures, and prettier re-pads
# every cell to align its pipes: a one-word edit to one row then rewrites the
# whole block (295 lines on PLAN-NOW.md alone). It also turns `*emphasis*` into
# `_emphasis_`. On files whose value IS the text, that trade is backwards.
*.md

# CAPTURED FROM UPSTREAM, so its shape is the provider's and not ours — the same
# argument design/ wins on. `assets-sample.json` is a trimmed live capture of
# Inzhur's `/_api/assets` (see src/core/README.md); reformatting it puts a
# whitespace diff on top of every re-capture and makes the refreshed file fail
# this very check.
src/**/__fixtures__/

# Machine-written, never hand-edited. Both lockfiles, because gating one and not
# the other is how `infra/package-lock.json` waits to fail on an npm version
# whose JSON prettier disagrees with.
pnpm-lock.yaml
infra/package-lock.json
